  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="59e0af3e-7aa3-5166-a07c-a495e98b2fbc" activityNameId="e1bb1bfd-11a4-53ee-b982-9fd7b41e61d4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Lignite briquette, burned in stove 5-15kW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Lignite briquette, burned in stove 5-15kW
The stove is assumed to fire lignite briquettes. The heating value (19.5 MJ/kg) and the composition of the briquettes are average values available from the literature. The emission data are also taken from literature reporting measurements performed at the end of the 1980s in Germany. Size distribution of particles has been estimated on the basis of recent information from EPA. Emissions of trace elements  were calculated using the ash content in the coal and average transfer coefficients for coal power plants with ash retention of 98 %, as first approximation.;
UUID: 634e0bcd-5c20-3b87-b21a-34009a8f294e
House heating. The module describes the combustion process and includes coal transport and ash disposal. 
Location: German conditions.
Technology: Average used in early 1990s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography/Text
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_634e0bcd-5c20-3b87-b21a-34009a8f294e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
